# Every text file is stored and checked out as LF. Without this, Windows editors and
# PowerShell rewrites turn a one-line edit into a whole-file diff, and `git diff` drowns
# in \r noise. The repository already stores LF; this pins it for every checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: content sniffing can misclassify small or text-like binaries, so state
# it explicitly and never apply eol conversion or a text diff to them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.db binary
